# Organizing Widgets with Frames

::: columns
:::: {.column width=50%}
- **Frame widget**: container that holds other widgets
  - Useful for organizing and arranging groups of widgets in a window
  - The contained widgets are added to the frame widget which contains them
  - Example: `tkinter.Label(self.top_frame, text='hi')`
::::
:::: {.column width=50%}
\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[scale=0.6]{figures/ch13-fig-13-19-frame-arrangement}
\label{fig:ch13-19-frame-arrangement}
\caption{Arrangement of widgets using a frame \parencite[pg.669]{gaddis-2021}}
\end{figure}
::::
:::

